        "original_id": "a9fb6765-e983-5fcd-ae3e-1e70a0de4b47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cocky\n- Concepts: Gamecock, cockfight, cockfighting\n- People: George Wilson\n- Works: The Commendation of Cocks and Cock Fighting\n\nFacts:\n- In 1607, George Wilson used the term \"cock of the game\" in The Commendation of Cocks and Cock Fighting, the earliest known book on the sport of cockfighting.\n- In 1634, the word \"gamecock\" was first documented as denoting use of the cock in a game, sport, pastime, or entertainment.\n- Cocky represents a cartoon version of a gamecock, which is a fighting rooster.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
